      "content": "Density in seawater is primarily determined by the temperature and salinity. As temperature increases, seawater's density also increases due to the higher thermal energy of water molecules. Conversely, salinity, which is the concentration of dissolved salts, also affects density, causing it to decrease upon increasing salinity. This is because dissolved salts increase the atomic mass of seawater, which increases its density.",
