      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, I think you might have flipped the temperature part. Doesn't higher temperature usually make water less dense? Anyway, I'm seeing some really strange spikes in the salinity readings at the 4000m mark in my data. They don't follow the expected thermohaline gradient at all. It looks like sensor noise or maybe some weird localized current, but the spikes are really erratic. Any idea what could cause such inconsistent readings in a stable trench environment?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
